Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/heal
Type: select
Choices: report, safe
Default: report
Description: What may the medic do by itself?
 report: say what it finds, in syslog and the rooms below, and change nothing.
 .
 safe: also run the remedies that are safe to run unasked: start a stopped
 Cassandra, Gitcha or nginx, restart a Gitcha that failed while its database
 was down.  A remedy that moves data or edits a file never runs by itself; a
 person runs it with: sudo gitcha-medic --yes NAME

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/channels
Type: multiselect
Choices: syslog, tavern, chadgram, webhook, c4
Default: syslog
Description: Where should the medic say what it finds?
 syslog: the host's own log (journalctl -t gitcha-medic).  tavern: a Tavern
 room on this machine.  chadgram: an ilmsg/1 JSONL file for a chad.tab route.
 webhook: any URL that takes JSON by POST (comic.chat and others, until they
 have adapters of their own).  c4: a folder postcards are dropped in.
 .
 The next questions ask for what each chosen channel needs.

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/tavern_agent_json
Type: string
Default: /var/lib/tavern/agent.json
Description: Tavern's agent.json on this machine:
 Tavern writes it in its data directory at each start: the local API port and
 the agent token.  The medic reads it per message and keeps no copy.

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/tavern_room
Type: string
Default: main
Description: Tavern room to speak in:

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/chadgram_file
Type: string
Default: /var/lib/gitcha-medic/chad.jsonl
Description: JSONL file for chadgram (one ilmsg/1 line per message):

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/webhook_url
Type: string
Default:
Description: Webhook URL (JSON by POST):

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/c4_dir
Type: string
Default:
Description: Folder to drop C4 postcards in:

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/agent
Type: select
Choices: none, claude, local, inputloop, openai
Default: none
Description: Which agent gives a second opinion?
 none: the rules alone.  claude: the Claude API (api.anthropic.com).
 .
 local, inputloop and openai are named but not written yet (TODO): an Ollama or
 llama-bridge endpoint, a Mentat or Tavern resident, an OpenAI-compatible
 server.  Choosing one now reserves the setting; the medic says so plainly
 until the adapter exists.
 .
 The agent sees redacted facts (no setting's value, no key) and may ask for the
 safe remedies only; it cannot say yes for a person.

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/agent_model
Type: string
Default: claude-opus-5-5
Description: Model name for that agent:

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/agent_url
Type: string
Default: https://api.anthropic.com
Description: Endpoint for that agent:

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/agent_key
Type: password
Description: API key for that agent:
 Written to /etc/inputloop/gitcha/agent.key (mode 600, root only), which the
 medic reads per call; not kept in the debconf database.  Leave it empty to
 keep the one already there, or when the endpoint needs none.

Template: inputloop-gitcha-medic/enable
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Run the medic every five minutes (gitcha-medic.timer)?
 If not now, later: systemctl enable --now gitcha-medic.timer
 By hand at any time: sudo gitcha-medic
